WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.071
- Welcome to Mom vs. Chef.

00:00:02.071 --> 00:00:03.628
A competition where a professional chef

00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:06.589
and a mom cook head-to-head,
preparing the best dish

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:08.818
possible with one super ingredient.

00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:12.025
(upbeat rock music)

00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:14.064
Our first competitor is Hannah WIlliams.

00:00:14.064 --> 00:00:16.205
- I'm Hannah, I'm a mother of two.

00:00:16.205 --> 00:00:18.135
I have a three-year-old
and a ten-month-old,

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:20.542
and I'm a home cook, I've
been cooking my whole life,

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:22.527
but I've never taken a cooking class.

00:00:22.527 --> 00:00:24.442
I used to check out recipe books

00:00:24.442 --> 00:00:26.603
from the library and bookmark them,

00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:29.424
do my nighttime reading, so I'm hoping

00:00:29.424 --> 00:00:31.531
that that helps me out
in this competition.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.940
I really wanna win today

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.032
because I want to make my kids proud.

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:36.719
When I left the house this morning,

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:39.945
my three-year-old told me
that I was a very good cookie

00:00:39.945 --> 00:00:42.519
and I think that meant "cook."

00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:43.859
He might of just meant "cookie"

00:00:43.859 --> 00:00:45.930
but if I can come home
and tell him that I cooked

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.178
something delicious, he's
gonna be so proud of me.

00:00:48.178 --> 00:00:49.711
- And competing against Hannah

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:52.739
is Professional Chef Steven Fretz.

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:53.819
- What's up, guys?

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:56.362
I'm Chef Steven Fretz, I'm
executive chef managing partner

00:00:56.362 --> 00:00:58.732
of The Church Key here in
Los Angeles, California.

00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:01.099
I've been cooking something like 21 years.

00:01:01.099 --> 00:01:03.503
I come from a higher-end background.

00:01:03.503 --> 00:01:05.661
We take on the world
cuisine, which we bring

00:01:05.661 --> 00:01:08.098
to America and call it
modern American cuisine.

00:01:08.098 --> 00:01:10.398
I have nine nieces and
nephews, I feel like

00:01:10.398 --> 00:01:12.882
I have some sort of ability
to cook for children.

00:01:12.882 --> 00:01:15.067
What would winning Mom
vs. Chef mean to me?

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.747
Well, bragging rights with my
three older sisters, right?

00:01:17.747 --> 00:01:19.418
- Welcome, Hannah, Chef Steven.

00:01:19.418 --> 00:01:20.581
Today you're gonna be competing

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:23.598
to make the tastiest dish
featuring one secret ingredient.

00:01:23.598 --> 00:01:25.339
Let me introduce you
to our panel of judges.

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:26.881
- Hi, I'm Kai and I'm six years

00:01:26.881 --> 00:01:28.910
old and I like playing my drums.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:32.410
- I'm Justin and I'm nine years
old and I like to do acting.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.257
- And your final judge is me.

00:01:34.257 --> 00:01:38.211
I'm Andrew, I'm 25 years
old, and I like race cars.

00:01:38.211 --> 00:01:39.444
So I think it's time to find out

00:01:39.444 --> 00:01:41.011
what the secret ingredient is.

00:01:41.011 --> 00:01:42.440
So Chefs, whatever you cook today

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.417
has to incorporate this secret ingredient.

00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.801
It is not going to be easy.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.048
Justin, will you do the honors, please?

00:01:48.048 --> 00:01:49.825
(suspenseful orchestral music)

00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:51.199
(groans)

00:01:51.199 --> 00:01:52.366
Guys know what this is?

00:01:52.366 --> 00:01:53.654
- It looks like horse poop.

00:01:53.654 --> 00:01:56.997
- So, chefs, today your
secret ingredient is spinach.

00:01:56.997 --> 00:01:58.670
- I was hopin' not to get something green

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.798
like broccoli or spinach
or something like that.

00:02:00.798 --> 00:02:02.205
- Hannah, how do you feel about spinach?

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.685
- Well, I've never met a kid who likes it.

00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:06.134
- Oh gosh, I don't want that.

00:02:06.134 --> 00:02:06.837
(hums)

00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:08.874
Chefs, you have 30
minutes to cook your food.

00:02:08.874 --> 00:02:10.372
- And your time starts.

00:02:10.372 --> 00:02:11.207
- Now.

00:02:11.207 --> 00:02:12.025
- Okay.

00:02:12.025 --> 00:02:13.403
- Spinach is one of the hardest things

00:02:13.403 --> 00:02:15.770
to get into a child, so I'm thinking,

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.207
"How can I incorporate this green color?"

00:02:18.207 --> 00:02:20.263
My mind immediately goes to one

00:02:20.263 --> 00:02:22.702
of my son's obsessions,
which is Minecraft.

00:02:22.702 --> 00:02:25.191
So I'm gonna make green
Creeper Minecraft pancakes

00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:28.256
with an egg frittata that is also green

00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:29.684
and I'm gonna turn that into a

00:02:29.684 --> 00:02:32.506
pixelated tree with a bacon trunk.

00:02:32.506 --> 00:02:34.335
- I've never put spinach in a kid dish.

00:02:34.335 --> 00:02:36.267
Generally at the
restaurant the big faux pas

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:38.513
is putting anything green on the dish.

00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:40.432
So what I think I'm gonna
do is I think I'm gonna go

00:02:40.432 --> 00:02:42.867
with something cheesy like
a cheesy alfredo sauce.

00:02:42.867 --> 00:02:45.136
Kids love cheesy, they love pasta,

00:02:45.136 --> 00:02:47.738
and I think it's a good way
to hide the spinach, right?

00:02:47.738 --> 00:02:50.807
- So I get my eggs in, I get
about a cup of spinach in,

00:02:50.807 --> 00:02:52.062
and I get a little bit of milk.

00:02:52.062 --> 00:02:53.297
This is gonna be for the frittata,

00:02:53.297 --> 00:02:55.700
and I blend the crud out of it until you

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.503
can't really see the spinach is in there.

00:02:57.503 --> 00:03:00.323
Hoping that I didn't overblend
it and this foam goes down.

00:03:00.323 --> 00:03:03.258
If it doesn't I'm just gonna
have to scrap this whole idea.

00:03:03.258 --> 00:03:04.338
- We'll probably just start off

00:03:04.338 --> 00:03:06.673
with sauteing the onions and some garlic.

00:03:06.673 --> 00:03:07.821
I don't know if kids like garlic

00:03:07.821 --> 00:03:08.865
but they're about to get some.

00:03:08.865 --> 00:03:11.268
Reduce that down with a
little bit of chicken stock.

00:03:11.268 --> 00:03:13.306
I think I found some cream and we'll

00:03:13.306 --> 00:03:14.838
just mount that with some cheese.

00:03:14.838 --> 00:03:16.876
Cut it with some acid from some lemon,

00:03:16.876 --> 00:03:19.453
and then hopefully we'll
be able to disguise

00:03:19.453 --> 00:03:21.803
the spinach the way we
need to for the kids.

00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:23.563
All right, I'm gonna
have a drink of water.

00:03:23.563 --> 00:03:25.722
- So the pancakes come off, taste them,

00:03:25.722 --> 00:03:27.741
it's a really overpowering
taste of spinach

00:03:27.741 --> 00:03:29.711
and it's not supposed to taste that way,

00:03:29.711 --> 00:03:32.862
and I'm hoping that the
judges are not gonna notice.

00:03:32.862 --> 00:03:33.942
- Hey, Chefs.

00:03:33.942 --> 00:03:36.828
- You have 15 minutes left, so hurry up.

00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:37.580
- [Steven] Uh oh.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.624
- [Hannah] I'm just starting.

00:03:39.624 --> 00:03:40.983
- How does that taste?

00:03:40.983 --> 00:03:41.702
(spits)

00:03:41.702 --> 00:03:42.970
- So what's your favorite food?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.180
- Pasta, salmon, broccoli.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.198
- I think my favorite food is steak.

00:03:47.198 --> 00:03:48.160
- Oh, I love steak.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.359
- So I'm lookin' over at Hannah

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:52.407
and I notice she had kids and
she understands the mindset

00:03:52.407 --> 00:03:56.639
of kids and she's putting
together this puzzle of a dish.

00:03:56.639 --> 00:03:59.981
I thought to myself, "This
is actually really smart."

00:03:59.981 --> 00:04:02.137
- I hope that they can translate this

00:04:02.137 --> 00:04:04.899
as the tree trunk because
this is all banking

00:04:04.899 --> 00:04:08.133
on the fact that these kids
know what Minecraft is.

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:10.029
Now, for the face on this pancake,

00:04:10.029 --> 00:04:12.694
I usually use blueberries to make a face.

00:04:12.694 --> 00:04:14.445
I go to the pantry and I don't see 'em.

00:04:14.445 --> 00:04:15.613
So I grab the chocolate chips.

00:04:15.613 --> 00:04:17.598
They're super hard, I
hope that the pancake

00:04:17.598 --> 00:04:19.758
is warm enough to melt it a little bit.

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:21.894
I'm just all over the place at this point

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.676
but it's too late to change my mind.

00:04:23.676 --> 00:04:25.173
- As I'm making my dish, I do think

00:04:25.173 --> 00:04:26.983
that the kids are gonna enjoy my dish.

00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:28.920
I'm feeling fairly confident that

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.864
I might have this under control.

00:04:30.864 --> 00:04:31.754
What's up, Kai?

00:04:31.754 --> 00:04:32.731
- What are you making?

00:04:32.731 --> 00:04:35.464
- I'm making a pasta
Alfredo sauce with bacon.

00:04:35.464 --> 00:04:36.382
We're gonna have spinach.

00:04:36.382 --> 00:04:37.118
- I knew it.

00:04:37.118 --> 00:04:38.251
- [Steven] And little bit of lemon

00:04:38.251 --> 00:04:39.868
and Parmesan cheese.
- [Kai] I was smelling bacon

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:40.579
over there.

00:04:40.579 --> 00:04:41.357
- [Steven] Yeah, right?

00:04:41.357 --> 00:04:42.707
I love bacon, I put bacon on everything.

00:04:42.707 --> 00:04:43.436
- Thanks, Chef.

00:04:43.436 --> 00:04:45.085
- [Steven] You're welcome.
- [Andrew] Hey, Hannah.

00:04:45.085 --> 00:04:45.905
- [Hannah] Hey.

00:04:45.905 --> 00:04:46.605
- How's it goin'?

00:04:46.605 --> 00:04:50.319
- I'm not quite sure what
boys this age are into,

00:04:50.319 --> 00:04:52.270
but I've heard a lot about Minecraft.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.090
- You know, I don't really
know that much about Minecraft,

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.797
so I feel like you shoulda catered

00:04:56.797 --> 00:04:58.172
toward my likes a little more.

00:04:58.172 --> 00:05:01.271
- I feel like you can appreciate themes.

00:05:01.271 --> 00:05:02.369
- We'll see if it works.

00:05:02.369 --> 00:05:03.140
(chuckles)

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:03.946
- Hey, Chef.

00:05:03.946 --> 00:05:04.979
- You have five minutes left.

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:06.339
- Oh boy, I better start plating.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.262
- Start wrappin' up.

00:05:07.262 --> 00:05:09.248
- While I'm cooking, I'm
thinking about my kids,

00:05:09.248 --> 00:05:12.330
I'm thinking about how
much they look up to me,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.151
and I'm hoping still that
I can make them proud,

00:05:15.151 --> 00:05:17.223
but seeing how things are going,

00:05:17.223 --> 00:05:19.242
I'm not feeling so good about myself.

00:05:19.242 --> 00:05:21.208
- Constantly I'm stirring the sauce

00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:23.688
to make sure it doesn't burn
right on the hot plates.

00:05:23.688 --> 00:05:27.972
Sometimes that direct
contact can burn your cheese.

00:05:27.972 --> 00:05:30.474
- Smelling Chef Steven's food is really

00:05:30.474 --> 00:05:32.007
putting a damper on everything.

00:05:32.007 --> 00:05:34.968
So at this point, whatever
it is, however it looks,

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:37.701
however it tastes, I just
want it to get on the plate.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:40.366
- [Andrew] Five, four, three,
- [Justin] Five, four, three,

00:05:40.366 --> 00:05:42.583
two, one.
- [Kai] two, one.

00:05:42.583 --> 00:05:45.800
Okay, stop working, Chefs,
the competition is over.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.473
We will now judge your dishes.

00:05:47.473 --> 00:05:48.533
- [Steven] Whew.

00:05:48.533 --> 00:05:50.449
- Hannah, can you please
describe your dish?

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:54.280
- What I made for you is
a Minecraft breakfast.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.756
When I think of spinach, I think of that

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:58.721
bright green color and when I think

00:05:58.721 --> 00:06:00.828
of bright green I think of the Creeper

00:06:00.828 --> 00:06:03.527
from Minecraft because my
son is obsessed with it.

00:06:03.527 --> 00:06:05.147
- Do you guys know what Minecraft is?

00:06:05.147 --> 00:06:05.892
- Yep.

00:06:05.892 --> 00:06:06.644
- I do.

00:06:06.644 --> 00:06:07.393
- I have the game.

00:06:07.393 --> 00:06:08.177
- Yes.

00:06:08.177 --> 00:06:11.661
So, you have a green Creeper pancake

00:06:11.661 --> 00:06:14.480
with chocolate chip face and a green egg

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:18.624
and bacon tree that's also
like the trees from the game.

00:06:18.624 --> 00:06:20.783
And I don't know what kind
of toppings you guys like

00:06:20.783 --> 00:06:22.999
on your pancakes so I
have some melted butter

00:06:22.999 --> 00:06:26.631
and syrup and I hope you enjoy it.

00:06:26.631 --> 00:06:27.643
- You love eggs?

00:06:27.643 --> 00:06:29.299
- Not really, but with salt.
- [Andrew] But it's a

00:06:29.299 --> 00:06:30.768
green egg.

00:06:30.768 --> 00:06:31.723
(groans)

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:33.268
Wow, there's a lot
- [Justin] It's really good.

00:06:33.268 --> 00:06:34.309
- [Andrew] of spinach in there.

00:06:34.309 --> 00:06:35.440
- It tastes like green kale.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:36.441
It's really good though.

00:06:36.441 --> 00:06:38.517
- Do I have a mustache?

00:06:38.517 --> 00:06:40.097
- Yeah, you have a little mustache there.

00:06:40.097 --> 00:06:42.081
I don't think you disguised the spinach

00:06:42.081 --> 00:06:43.632
as much as you thought you would

00:06:43.632 --> 00:06:46.804
in the pancakes, but as a spinach bread

00:06:46.804 --> 00:06:48.890
kind of thing, it's actually really nice.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:49.938
- I like the bacon.

00:06:49.938 --> 00:06:51.177
- The only thing I didn't really like

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.931
was the chocolate chips.

00:06:52.931 --> 00:06:56.257
The chocolate and spinach is
a little weird combination.

00:06:56.257 --> 00:06:57.336
Thank you, Hannah.

00:06:57.336 --> 00:06:58.207
- Thank you.

00:06:58.207 --> 00:07:00.872
- Chef Steven, can you please
tell us about the dish?

00:07:00.872 --> 00:07:04.060
- I went with the cheesy
goodness of pasta,

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:08.953
so I made a bacon Alfredo sauce
with a little bit of garlic,

00:07:08.953 --> 00:07:11.310
some onions, a little bit of lemon,

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:14.958
and then a lot of Parmesan
cheese, sour cream, and cream.

00:07:14.958 --> 00:07:16.160
And then you have your spinach

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.007
just at the end, it was folded in.

00:07:18.007 --> 00:07:18.717
Please enjoy.

00:07:18.717 --> 00:07:19.957
- What about the spinach in there?

00:07:19.957 --> 00:07:22.390
It's not as disguised as Hannah's was.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:25.860
- I could taste a hint of
lemon and it's really good.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:28.732
- It's very tasty.

00:07:28.732 --> 00:07:29.982
Honestly, I wish the spinach

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.202
was coming through a little more.

00:07:31.202 --> 00:07:32.978
- The spinach is not helping the dish.

00:07:32.978 --> 00:07:34.841
- Thanks for everything, Chef and Hannah.

00:07:34.841 --> 00:07:35.650
- Thanks, guys.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.773
- Thank you.
- [Steven] Thank you.

00:07:36.773 --> 00:07:39.581
- [Justin] Chef and Hannah,
we need a moment to decide.

00:07:39.581 --> 00:07:40.373
- So spinach, huh?

00:07:40.373 --> 00:07:41.764
What did you think?
- [Hannah] Oh my gosh.

00:07:41.764 --> 00:07:43.246
Kids are just unpredictable.

00:07:43.246 --> 00:07:44.855
- [Steven] You know, I'm
not feelin' really good

00:07:44.855 --> 00:07:46.212
about what they thought so far.

00:07:46.212 --> 00:07:48.493
- I keep thinking back, I should
of put less spinach in it,

00:07:48.493 --> 00:07:50.410
it still would of been
green, and it wouldn't

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:51.607
of tasted so much like spinach.

00:07:51.607 --> 00:07:53.122
It's just so rushed.
- [Steven] Your point was

00:07:53.122 --> 00:07:54.190
to use spinach, you know?

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.618
That's what they gave us to use.

00:07:55.618 --> 00:07:59.214
I just wanted to make it
cheesy, we'll see what happens.

00:07:59.214 --> 00:08:00.701
- [Hannah] I feel like
it's a total toss-up.

00:08:00.701 --> 00:08:02.164
- So who did you think did a better job?

00:08:02.164 --> 00:08:03.627
- I think Steve.

00:08:03.627 --> 00:08:04.778
- I think Hannah.

00:08:04.778 --> 00:08:07.550
Because of the eggs, I didn't really taste

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.418
the spinach in it even though I ate it.

00:08:10.418 --> 00:08:13.623
- Chef Steven had little bacon bits.

00:08:13.623 --> 00:08:15.451
- Yeah, it was very tasty.

00:08:15.451 --> 00:08:16.531
- Which one do you think?

00:08:16.531 --> 00:08:18.917
- I don't know, they both had good things

00:08:18.917 --> 00:08:20.853
and not so good things.
- [Kai] I think both.

00:08:20.853 --> 00:08:21.789
- [Andrew] Both are good?

00:08:21.789 --> 00:08:22.521
- Mmhmm.

00:08:22.521 --> 00:08:23.457
- Well, only one can win.

00:08:23.457 --> 00:08:24.541
- Let's bring them back in.

00:08:24.541 --> 00:08:26.579
- I could see a little bit of hair

00:08:26.579 --> 00:08:27.727
sticking out of your nose.

00:08:27.727 --> 00:08:29.974
- Chef Steven, Hannah, thank you,

00:08:29.974 --> 00:08:31.719
you prepared some amazing food today.

00:08:31.719 --> 00:08:33.544
Unfortunately, we can
only have one winner.

00:08:33.544 --> 00:08:36.627
- Chef Steven, your food was tasty,

00:08:36.627 --> 00:08:40.106
but Hannah, I think your food was tastier.

00:08:40.106 --> 00:08:42.319
- [Hannah] Oh my gosh.

00:08:42.319 --> 00:08:43.592
Oh my gosh.

00:08:43.592 --> 00:08:45.680
- Hannah, you're the first winner

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:47.998
of Mom vs. Chef, congratulations.

00:08:47.998 --> 00:08:50.427
(squeals)
(clapping)

00:08:50.427 --> 00:08:54.405
- I was not expecting to
win at all so I'm still

00:08:54.405 --> 00:08:57.685
in shock I think, they announced my name

00:08:57.685 --> 00:08:59.979
that I won and I just started shaking.

00:08:59.979 --> 00:09:03.287
- I came here because my two sons think

00:09:03.287 --> 00:09:05.254
that I'm a really good cook and I wanted

00:09:05.254 --> 00:09:08.076
to prove them right, I wanted
to show that I could do it.

00:09:08.076 --> 00:09:08.931
- I love it.

00:09:08.931 --> 00:09:10.007
